   "source": [
    "# Stock Portfolio Analyzer with AI Insights\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook analyzes a sample stock portfolio using Python and real market data from Yahoo Finance. It calculates returns, risk, volatility, allocation, correlation, Sharpe ratio, and portfolio-level takeaways.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Example portfolio:** AAPL, MSFT, NVDA, JPM, XOM  \n",
    "**Starting investment:** $10,000\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Project Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "The goal of this project is to evaluate how a stock portfolio performed historically and explain the results in simple business language. The notebook uses market data, calculates key investment metrics, and creates charts that make the portfolio easier to understand.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Real-World Finance Use Case\n",
    "\n",
    "A financial analyst can use this type of workflow to review a portfolio, compare risk across holdings, identify the strongest and weakest stocks, and summarize the results for investors or managers.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Required Python Libraries\n",
    "\n",
    "This project uses:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `yfinance` for stock price data\n",
    "- `pandas` for data analysis\n",
    "- `numpy` for calculations\n",
    "- `matplotlib` and `plotly` for charts\n",
    "- `seaborn` for the correlation heatmap\n",
    "\n",
    "Run the setup cell below first in Google Colab."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Install yfinance in Google Colab\n",
    "!pip install yfinance --quiet\n",
    "\n",
    "# Import required libraries\n",
    "import yfinance as yf\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "import plotly.express as px\n",
    "import plotly.graph_objects as go\n",
    "\n",
    "# Make charts look cleaner\n",
    "plt.rcParams['figure.figsize'] = (12, 6)\n",
    "plt.rcParams['axes.grid'] = True\n",
    "\n",
    "# Display settings\n",
    "pd.set_option('display.float_format', lambda x: f'{x:,.4f}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Google Colab Setup\n",
    "\n",
